G1.2  persistence of the prescribed target (v = 0 at t0): Lagrangian shells, Newtonian, pre-crossing; the flow is class-independent (T0.3a)
==============================================================================================================
  each shell i has Lagrangian mass coordinate mu_in,i = mu_T(s0_i) and falls radially; ordering holds until the inner shell reaches the centre (radial fall from rest),
  so the first shell crossing at x is bracketed by T_ff(s0_i) <= t_cross,i <= T_ff(s0_{i+1}); the class-C source (beta = -gamma) does not move the shells (only the density along them).
