G1.3  pressureless-static identity: p_eff = 0 => the target is static iff f_ext = g_tot (outward) at every r
==============================================================================================================
  exponential sphere: g_tot(target)/g_law(P2) over x in [0.1, 30]: min 0.800, max 0.999 (reported)
  [PASS] G1.3a  point mass: f_ext/g_law = g_tot(target)/g_law(P2) = 1 identically (P2: g = sqrt(g_N^2 + a0 g_N) IS the target's g_tot)
         measured: max |f_ext/g_law - 1| = 4.4e-16
  [FAIL] G1.3b  with no external force the resting target dust accelerates inward at a_res = g_tot (order g_law) at every x; a static state needs f_ext = g_tot
         measured: a_res/g_law: point mass min 1.000 max 1.000
  corollary (structural): f_ext = g_tot(total) cancels the dust's gravity inside bound systems; in the linear regime at z >~ 10 the dust must feel gravity (G2). The coupling therefore has to switch: Gap 1's owner switch.

